{{also|wüste}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wüeste}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wuostī}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*wōstį̄}}. Equivalent to {{affix|de|wüst|-e}}. Also merged with {{m+|gmh|wüestene}}, from {{m+|goh|wuostin}}, {{m|goh||*wuostinna}}, from {{m+|gmw-pro|*wōstini}} (through regular reduction of feminines in ''-en(e)'' to ''-e'', compare {{m|de|Küche}} etc.). The latter is cognate with {{cog|nl|woestijn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvyːstə/}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Wü|ste}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Wüs|te}}
* {{audio|de|De-Wüste.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# [[desert]]
# [[wilderness]], [[waste]], [[wasteland]]
#* '''1844''', [[w:Felix Mendelssohn|Felix Mendelssohn]], ''[[w:Hear my Prayer|Hör' mein Bitten]]'' (with literal translation):
#*: {{quote|de|O könnt' ich fliegen wie Tauben dahin,<br> weit hinweg vor dem Feinde zu fliehn!<br> In die '''Wüste''' eilt' ich dann fort,<br> fände Ruhe am schattigen Ort.|Oh, if I could fly off like the doves,<br> flee far away from the foe!<br>Into the '''wilderness''' I would then hasten,<br> and find repose in a shadowy place.}}

